WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.720
How could you multiply nine with eight?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.780
Some of you have probably memorised

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.440
the multiples of nine and know the answer.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.240
We know that it is 72, but in this session,

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.420
we will understand multiplication in a very different way,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.540
Will this different way help us?

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.040
Well, let me put it this way.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:31.700
Understanding this technique will help us solve problems

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.640
like 'nine hundred ninety eight' times 'nine hundred ninety seven' in about five seconds.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.320
Yes, without a calculator.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.560
You don't believe me do you ?

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.840
Give me around two minutes to change your opinion!

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.320
We use the concept of base to solve multiplication problems quickly!

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:54.080
and bases are generally powers of Ten, like 10,

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.480
100,1000 and so on.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.460
When we are given the multiplication problem, the first thing

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:05.660
we should ask ourselves is 'which base is close to both the numbers?'

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.040
Here, both numbers are close to ten. So we can say that the base is ten.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:15.440
Once the base is decided, life becomes really easy.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:18.780
First, we subtract the base from each of these numbers!

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.240
Subtracting the base from the first number,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.700
we get '9 minus 10' that equals minus one.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.260
We write it next to that number.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.560
Next would be '8 minus 10', that equals minus 2.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.560
These two numbers tell us how far these two numbers are from the base.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.460
9 is 'minus one units' away from the base.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.280
and 8 is 'minus two units' away from the base.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:48.500
So the initial two steps: choose the base, and subtract it from the numbers.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:53.460
Once this is done, just make a partition like this. On the left,

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.460
we write the sum.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:00.080
What sum? The sum of these two numbers or these two numbers!

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:02.880
Both will result in the same answer!

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.540
Either 8 plus 'minus 1', or 9 plus ‘minus 2’. Both equals 7.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:11.100
So we write a 7 on the left.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.380
On the right, we have the product of these two numbers!

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.980
'minus 1 multiplied by minus 2'. And that equals 2.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.680
Yes, we should also consider the sign when multiplied these two numbers.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.960
There you go. We have the answer '9 times 8' is 72.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.660
The steps are simple: we find the base,

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.060
then subtract it from each number,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.060
write the sum on the left and the product on the right.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.820
Is there anything we need to be careful about here?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.100
Yes, on the right, the number of digits,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.500
should be equal to the number of zeros in the base!

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.380
Here, the base has one zero, so we write just one digit on the right.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:57.000
Don't worry... everybody thinks this is difficult at first.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.580
So let's quickly solve a couple of problems

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:03.620
and you will see how simple this technique actually is!

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.600
Say we want to multiply '98 with 97'.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.780
Both these numbers as we can see are close to 100.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.220
So the base is 100 here.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.200
98 minus 100 is 'minus 2' and

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:23.280
97 minus 100 is 'minus 3'. Then we make a partition.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.040
On the left we write the sum and on the right, we write the product.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:35.600
98 plus 'minus 3' is 95. Even 97 plus 'minus 2' will give us 95.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.820
And 'minus 2 times minus 3' is 6.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.060
So should we write a 6 here?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.480
Don't forget,

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.500
the number of digits on the right will be equal to the number of zeros in the base!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:52.160
As there are 2 zeros and 100 ,there will be 2 digits here.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.760
6 will be written as '06'.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.900
There's your answer!

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:02.300
'98 times 97' is  9506.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.980
Find the base, find the deviation,

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.900
find the sum and find the product and we get the answer in a few seconds!

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.240
Okay, let's try solving a problem with slightly bigger numbers.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:23.340
9996 times 9997. Why don't you try this?

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.920
Remember the four simple steps.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.960
Find the base, find the deviation ,

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.360
find the sum and find the product.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.340
I give you 'ten seconds'.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:50.040
Both numbers as we can see are close to '10,000', so the base will be 10,000.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:56.240
This number is 'minus 4' units away, and this is 'minus 3' units away.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.280
Then we make the partition. Sum on the left and the product on the right!

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:06.120
This plus this is 9993.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.280
The sum of these two will also give us

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:10.760
9993.

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:16.000
The product will be 'minus 4 times minus 3' which equals twelve.

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:18.520
The number of zeros in the base is four,

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.780
which means we will have four digits on the right.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.580
12 will be written as' zero zero one two'.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.140
That's our answer.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:32.320
The product of these two numbers will equal 'Nine Nine Nine three zero zero one two'.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.360
Wasn't this quick?

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.880
Faster than a calculator you think?

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.200
Notice that in all the examples we saw,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.900
both numbers were below the base.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:45.740
98 and 97 were below 100.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.980
9996

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.520
and 9997

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.600
were below 10,000.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.740
We will look at a couple of more examples in the next part of the session.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:58.660
Don't forget the steps:

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.140
Find the base, find the deviation,

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.160
find the sum and find the product.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.100
And we get the answer!

